        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(acp): close shared state database on gateway shutdown (#100637)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #100637: The standalone ACP gateway process (`serveAcpGateway`) opens a SQLite `DatabaseSync` connection through `createSqliteAcpEventLedger()` but never closes it on SIGINT/SIGTERM shutdown. This leaks file descriptors and causes SQLite file locking issues during hot reload.\n\nAdditionally, steipete identified a race condition in the original fix: `onEvent` fires `handleGatewayEvent` without tracking its promise. If SIGINT arrives while a handler is in-flight (suspended on `connection.sessionUpdate`), the handler could resume after shutdown and reopen the cached SQLite handle via `openOpenClawStateDatabase`.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n1. `src/acp/server.ts` shutdown handler only called `gateway.stop()` — never called `closeOpenClawStateDatabase()`\n2. `onEvent` used `void` to discard the `handleGatewayEvent` promise — no tracking of in-flight handlers\n3. `onClosed()` was called synchronously inside `gateway.stop()` → `onClose` callback, before any drain or DB close\n\n## Changes\n\n- `src/acp/server.ts`:\n  - Import `closeOpenClawStateDatabase` from shared state DB module\n  - Track in-flight `handleGatewayEvent` promises in a `Set<Promise<void>>`\n  - Skip new events in `onEvent` when shutdown has started\n  - In `shutdown()`: drain in-flight handlers via `Promise.allSettled` before closing the shared state DB\n  - Move `onClosed()` out of the `onClose` callback so the shutdown promise resolves after drain+close, not during `gateway.stop()`\n- `src/acp/server.startup.test.ts`:\n  - Add test proving DB close on shutdown (13 → 14 tests)\n  - Add regression test: suspend `sessionUpdate`, trigger shutdown, verify DB is NOT closed while handler is in-flight, then resolve and verify DB IS closed after drain\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Tests (14/14 pass)\n\n```\n$ pnpm test src/acp/server.startup.test.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  14 passed (14)\n\n$ pnpm test src/acp/event-ledger.test.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  12 passed (12)\n\n$ pnpm test src/state/openclaw-state-db.test.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  18 passed (18)\n```\n\n### Race condition regression test\n\nThe new test \"drains in-flight gateway events before closing the shared state database on shutdown\":\n1. Creates a deferred promise that suspends `handleGatewayEvent`\n2. Fires a gateway event → handler begins, promise tracked in `inFlightEvents`\n3. Triggers SIGINT shutdown\n4. **Assert**: `closeOpenClawStateDatabase` has NOT been called (handler still in-flight)\n5. Resolves the deferred → handler completes\n6. **Assert**: `closeOpenClawStateDatabase` was called exactly once (after drain)\n\n### Diff scope\n\n```\n src/acp/server.startup.test.ts | 55 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--\n src/acp/server.ts              | 26 ++++++++++++---------\n 2 files changed, 70 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)\n```\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
